---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
---
<SiteLayout title="Privacy Policy — Toolora" description="Learn how Toolora handles your information and processes files and text in your browser.">
  <SiteHeader backHref="/" backLabel="Home" />
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Privacy</div><span class="eyebrow">Privacy & transparency</span><h1 class="display text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold mt-3">Privacy Policy</h1><p class="text-slate-500 mt-3 text-sm max-w-2xl">Your content should stay yours. This page explains how Toolora handles information when you use the website.</p></div></section>
    <section class="section"><article class="container max-w-3xl tool-panel p-6 md:p-9">
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: November 25, 2026</p>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl font-bold mt-7">1. Content you process</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">Toolora is designed to process text and selected files directly in your browser wherever the tool supports local processing. Toolora does not intentionally upload the content you enter or the files you select to a Toolora application server for processing.</p>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl font-bold mt-7">2. Community submissions</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">When community features are enabled, you may submit a tool review (display name, star rating and review text) or a tool request (tool name and description). These submissions are stored in a Cloudflare D1 database controlled by the site owner and remain pending until manually moderated. Only approved reviews are shown publicly. Do not include sensitive or confidential information in a submission. The service applies basic abuse-prevention rate limits using a one-way digest of the connecting IP address; raw IP addresses are not stored in the community database. Submissions may be retained until removed by the site owner.</p>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl font-bold mt-7">3. Third-party services</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">The QR code tool loads a version-pinned open-source library from cdnjs only when you use that tool. The CDN provider may receive technical request information such as your IP address and browser details when your browser connects to it; the text or URL you encode is processed locally and is not sent to the CDN. PDF creation and PDF rendering libraries are bundled with Toolora and run in your browser. Toolora uses system fonts and does not request Google Fonts. Toolora is hosted on Cloudflare infrastructure, which may process technical request data for delivery, reliability and security. The providers’ own privacy terms apply to their services.</p>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl font-bold mt-7">4. Browser permissions and downloads</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">Copying results, downloading generated files and text-to-speech playback use browser capabilities. These actions are initiated by you and remain subject to your browser settings and permissions.</p>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl font-bold mt-7">5. Cookies, accounts and analytics</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">Toolora does not currently require an account to use its tools. No account password or file upload is collected by the community API. If analytics, accounts, advertising or other data collection features are introduced, this policy should be updated before those features are enabled.</p>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl font-bold mt-7">6. Changes</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">This policy may be updated as Toolora's features and infrastructure change. Please review this page periodically.</p>
    </article></section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</SiteLayout>
